{
  "id": "21357_sonemu",
  "headword": "{嫉|そね}む",
  "reading": "そねむ",
  "romaji": "sonemu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to envy; to be jealous of; to begrudge",
  "verb_type": "godan",
  "verb_ending": "む",
  "transitivity": "transitive",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to envy; to be jealous of; to begrudge",
      "explanation": "To feel resentful envy toward someone because of their success, talent, or good fortune."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21357_sonemu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{他人|たにん}の{成功|せいこう}を{嫉|そね}む。",
      "english": "To envy others' success.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21357_sonemu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{才能|さいのう}のある{人|ひと}を{嫉|そね}んではいけない。",
      "english": "You shouldn't be jealous of talented people.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21357_sonemu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{周囲|しゅうい}から{嫉|そね}まれるほど{美|うつく}しかった。",
      "english": "She was so beautiful that people around her envied her.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Carries a stronger negative connotation than {羨|うらや}ましい, implying resentment or spite rather than simple admiration. The envy described by {嫉|そね}む is often bitter and can lead to hostility. Used primarily in written or literary contexts; in everyday speech, {妬|ねた}む is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}の{幸|しあわ}せを{嫉|そね}む: to begrudge others' happiness\n- {成功|せいこう}を{嫉|そね}む: to be envious of someone's success\n- {嫉|そね}まれる: to be envied (passive)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {妬|ねた}む: to be jealous of, to envy — more common in everyday speech, similar intensity\n- {嫉妬|しっと}する: to feel jealousy — the する-verb form, used broadly for both romantic and non-romantic jealousy\n- {羨|うらや}む: to envy — lighter, can be admiring rather than resentful",
